 of embryos cloned from donor cells treated by trichostatin A or 5-aza-2'-deoxycytidine</article-title><source>Biol Reprod</source><year>2003</year><volume>69</volume><fpage>896</fpage><lpage>901</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12748129</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Everts</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Tian</surname><given-names>XC</given-names></name><name><surname>Du</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Sung</surname><given-names>LY</given-names></name><name><surname>Rodriguez-Zas</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Jeong</surname><given-names>BS</given-names></name><name><surname>Renard</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Lewin</surname><given-names>HA</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Global gene expression profiles reveal significant nuclear reprogramming by the blastocyst stage after cloning</article-title><source>Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America</source><year>2005</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>17582</fpage><lpage>17587</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16314565</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Somers</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Donnison</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Wells</surname><given-names>DN</given-names></name><name><surname>Henderson</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>McLeay</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfeffer</surname><given-names>PL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Gene exp